From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: report MSM8226 chained GPIO effective affinity

MSM8226 GPIO interrupts are demultiplexed by the TLMM summary interrupt.
Their effective affinity is otherwise empty, so CPU hotplug assumes
every CPU in the default mask can receive them and attempts impossible
independent GPIO migrations. System suspend logs repeated set-affinity
failures.

Accept a requested mask when it already contains the summary IRQ's
actual target, and report that effective target. Keep rejecting requests
which would require independent routing, and leave direct-connect IRQs
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c
@@ -1300,6 +1300,20 @@
 	if (d->parent_data && test_bit(d->hwirq, pctrl->skip_wake_irqs))
 		return irq_chip_set_affinity_parent(d, dest, force);
 
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(pctrl->dev->of_node, "qcom,msm8226-pinctrl")) {
+		struct irq_data *parent = irq_get_irq_data(pctrl->irq);
+		const struct cpumask *effective;
+
+		/* Chained GPIOs execute on the summary IRQ's actual target. */
+		if (!parent)
+			return -EINVAL;
+		effective = irq_data_get_effective_affinity_mask(parent);
+		if (!cpumask_empty(effective) && cpumask_subset(effective, dest)) {
+			irq_data_update_effective_affinity(d, effective);
+			return IRQ_SET_MASK_OK_DONE;
+		}
+	}
+
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
